      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I also encountered this issue.\nNormalizing probabilities routine of VRC_TriggerEditor has a defect.\n\nSteps to reproduce 100%:\n--------\n1. Make new trigger entry. Add two actions. (Referred to as X and Y)\n2. Check on advanced mode and check on Randomize checkbox\n3. Set probability 1.0 to X\n4. Using text field, set probability 1.0 to Y\n5. Then Unity Editor doesn't respond any more.\n\nWorkaround:\n--------\n* Avoid a situation in which sum of probabilities is over 1.0.\n* Decline other action probability before rising up another one.\n\nCause:\n--------\n\"Do not use floating-point variables as loop counters\". See https://wiki.sei.cmu.edu/confluence/display/c/FLP30-C.+Do+not+use+floating-point+variables+as+loop+counters\n\nIn RenderTriggerEventsEditor function of VRC_TriggerEditor,\ndo-while loop uses \"sum of probability > 1.0\" to continue. (Around commented \"Squish 'em down\")\nIt will become almost nearly 1.0 but remains as \"higher than 1.0\". It brings infinite busy loop for Unity Editor.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
